# WHERE the framework collaborator's own stores live — the event Log
# (EventSourcing::Event), the veto audit (Governance::Violation) and the
# event-out outbox (OutboundEvent).
#
# The runtime writes these three ; a user's domain never carries them. They used
# to land wherever the booted app's data happened to go, by INHERITANCE — the
# collaborator simply cloned its parent's data_dir. That produced the right
# location for the wrong reason : an accident nobody had declared, which no
# reader could look up.
#
# `dir :default` is that same location, now DECLARED : the framework store sits
# in the SAME FOLDER as the host application's persistence. Per-project by
# construction — a deployed app gets its own storehouse, so it gets its own
# framework store, and two projects on one dev machine can never drain each
# other's outbound queue.
#
# This file is CRATE-OWNED (rust/resources/) and compiled in, because storehouse
# must build standalone with no sibling hecks_conception. That also keeps it out
# of reach of `apply_per_domain_world_dirs`, which keys on `category` and would
# otherwise match the ~48 conception bluebooks that also declare
# `category "framework"`.
Hecks.world "Framework" do
  persisted_by("Heki") do
    dir :default
  end
end
